      "writtenOn": "2024-01-16T08:32:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the rialto footer is added with `AddHashFooter`, `check_resigned_image_avb_info` is indeed invoked, but that\u0027s different with the checks here.\n\n`check_resigned_image_avb_info` mostly asserts that updated_value \u003d\u003d original_value, but it doesn\u0027t compare the content to a specific value. For example,\n\n\u003e len(updated_descriptors) / len(updated_prop) / len(updated_hash_descriptors)\n\nIf somehow the number of original prop or descriptors is 0 or 3, `check_resigned_image_avb_info` will also pass, but for rialto I want to be sure that there are 2 descriptors with 1 hash and 1 prop.\n\n\u003e updated_info[\"Rollback Index\"] !\u003d \"0\"\n\n`check_resigned_image_avb_info` doesn\u0027t check that rollback index is not 0. Both original and updated can be 0 \n\n\u003e assert_different_value(original_descriptor, updated_descriptor, \"Digest\"..\n\nThe digest is ignored in `check_resigned_image_avb_info` because it depends on callers\u0027 policy.",
